// In_SOC FPGA hardware demo firmware -- BIST self-test, no external ADC.
// 256 x 16-bit words. Same reset vector / arc-ISR / main-startup / timer-ISR
// layout as the default cpu_program.hex (0x00-0x09, unchanged), only the old
// "0x08: JMP 0x08" idle loop is redirected into the demo sequence below.
//
// This is a SEPARATE image from firmware/cpu_program.hex on purpose: it is
// selected only for Quartus synthesis (via the ROM_INIT_FILE set_parameter
// override in In_SOC.qsf) and must never become the default image loaded by
// the Questa regressions -- verified experimentally that this firmware's
// BIST trigger genuinely trips dsp_arc_detect's fire condition (LFSR seed
// 0xACE1 against the default profile), which reads as a false-positive arc
// trip to tb_professional's Scenario 1 if loaded there. See review notes /
// tb_fpga_demo_check.sv for the simulation evidence.
//
// 0x00: JMP  0x04
// 0x01: STR  R0, 0x20        Arc ISR
// 0x02: STR  R0, 0x28        Arc ISR
// 0x03: JMP  0x03            Arc ISR (halt, awaits reset)
// 0x04: LDI  R0, 0x01
// 0x05: STR  R0, 0x20
// 0x06: LDI  R0, 0x00
// 0x07: STR  R0, 0x28
// 0x08: JMP  0x0A            was "JMP 0x08" idle loop; now enters BIST demo
// 0x09: RET                  timer ISR (unused, kept as convention placeholder)
//
// --- BIST self-test demo (0x0A-0x10) ---
// logic_bist injects a real LFSR stimulus stream into dsp_arc_detect.
// Verified via simulation that the default seed/test-length genuinely trips
// the DSP's fire condition. The masked irq_arc_critical unmasks the moment
// BIST leaves RUN, so the CPU is preempted straight into the existing arc
// ISR (0x01-0x03, unmodified) -- this demo intentionally rides that real
// safety path end-to-end (BIST -> real DSP trip -> CPU NMI -> relay/GPIO
// latch) instead of trying to dodge it:
//   0x0A: LDI  R6, 0x0F      GPIO PADDIR = all 4 pins output
//   0x0B: STR  R6, 0x20      GPIO.PADDIR = R6
//   0x0C: LDI  R6, 0x04      DATAOUT: bit2 status LED ON ("self-test running")
//   0x0D: STR  R6, 0x28      GPIO.DATAOUT = R6
//   0x0E: LDI  R6, 0x01      BIST.CTRL start value
//   0x0F: STR  R6, 0x60      BIST.CTRL = R6  (self-clearing start bit)
//   0x10: JMP  0x10          idle; the arc-trip preemption interrupts this
//                            asynchronously within a few dozen cycles
// From here control never returns to 0x10: the CPU lands in the pre-existing
// arc ISR (drives GPIO, then halts at 0x03 by design) exactly as it would
// for a genuine arc fault. Press the board reset button to reboot and
// re-arm the self-test for another run.
5004 7020 7028 5003 1001 7020 1000 7028 500A F000 1C0F 7C20 1C04 7C28 1C01 7C60
